cmu-mohawk-floor = Mohawk deck
cmu-mohawk-roof = Mohawk upper hull plating
cmu-mohawk-ramp = Mohawk boarding ramp
cmu-mohawk-camera-omaha = Omaha cameras
cmu-mohawk-camera-midway = Midway cameras
cmu-mohawk-flight-interlock = The flight interlock prevents deploying the ramp or ladder.
cmu-mohawk-landing-obstructed = The landing site does not have clearance for all three decks.
cmu-mohawk-controls-no-access = Access denied. Only pilots, engineers, and command can operate the ramp and ladder.
cmu-mohawk-controls-broken = The remote connection is damaged. Repair it with a multitool.
cmu-mohawk-controls-unskilled = You need engineering or piloting training to repair these controls.
cmu-mohawk-controls-sabotaged = The controls spark as the hatch is forced open!
cmu-mohawk-controls-repaired = The remote connection has been restored.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-only = Fire the M90 from the dedicated gunnery console.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-seat = You must be buckled into the gunnery seat to fire the M90.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-manual = Take turret control
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-automatic = Release / close defense
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-control-help = Take control while seated and landed or during a CAS flyby. Move the mouse over the left camera to aim; hold left click for continuous fire at three explosive shells or ten Squall kinetic rounds per second. Arrows pan; the center button recenters. Mark a hostile, then Authorize fire for thirty seconds. During a flyby, select an active signal flare on the right TARGET monitor: shells produce delayed impacts within ten tiles of it, not travelling projectiles. Flare targeting is unavailable while landed or hovering. Select feed 1/2 or toggle alternating feeds. AI free fire automatically engages hostiles for 120 seconds, then has a five-minute cooldown. Unmanned landed close defense engages hostiles within four tiles. Friendly-fire checks still apply. At zero integrity the M90 disables and requires a staged engineer rebuild.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-ground-only = Manual chin-gun control requires landing or an active CAS flyby; it is unavailable during transit, takeoff or tactical hover.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-ammo-ground-only = Squall kinetic ammunition is groundside-only. Select an explosive feed for airborne fire.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-busy = Another operator is controlling the chin turret.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-out-of-range = The target is outside the chin turret's range.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-out-of-arc = The target is behind the chin turret's forward firing arc.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-auth-expired = Fire authorization expired. Confirm the target again to resume.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-unsafe-shot = Holding fire: a friendly or an opaque obstruction is in the firing path.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-flare-invalid = Flare targeting requires an active CAS flyby and a selected active signal flare. Aim within ten tiles of that flare. Clearing the flare disables airborne fire.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-mark-help = Press this button, then click a visible hostile in the left camera. Marking never authorizes fire.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-mark-pending = Click a hostile in the left camera.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-unmarked = No marked target.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-acquire = Acquire priority target
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-acquire-help = Mark the nearest or highest-health visible hostile, according to the priority setting. With a flare selected, acquire only within ten tiles of it. Then authorize fire separately.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-authorize = Authorize fire (30 seconds)
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-authorize-help = Mark or acquire a hostile first. Authorizes that entity for thirty seconds, firing only while visible and safe.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-priority-distance = Priority: nearest
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-priority-health = Priority: highest health
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-clear-flare = Clear flare / recenter
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-pan-help = Pan two tiles with the arrows. The center button recenters on the flare or chin mount. Panning clears tracking and authorization.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-short-help = Mouse: aim | Hold click: fire
    Mark -> Authorize: tracked fire
    Arrows: pan | Center: recenter
    Flyby TARGET: select a flare
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-airborne-flare-only = Airborne M90 fire requires an active CAS flyby and a selected signal flare. Landed fire uses physical shells; tactical hover does not support flare fire.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-airborne-preview = Flyby fire: ten tiles around the flare | Impact delay: 1-2 seconds | Three shells per second
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-airburst-blocked = Holding fire: the dispersed impact is outside the flare area, under protected cover, or too close to a friendly.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-airburst-cancelled = A delayed M90 impact was cancelled because friendly clearance was lost. The released shell remains consumed.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-feed-selected = Feed mode: selected
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-feed-alternate = Feed mode: alternate each shell
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-feed-select = Feed {$feed} {$active}
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-feed-ammo = {$ammo} ({$rounds} rounds)
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-feed-empty = empty
cmu-mohawk-free-fire-enable = AI free fire (120 seconds)
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-disabled = M90 disabled: requires a complete rebuild.
cmu-mohawk-gunnery-health = M90 integrity: {$health}/{$max} HP
cmu-mohawk-repair-grounded = The dropship must be grounded to rebuild the M90.
cmu-mohawk-repair-strip = Disabled M90: use a wrench to strip the damaged mechanism (20 seconds).
cmu-mohawk-repair-parts = Disabled M90: install one box of 90mm repair parts (120 seconds).
cmu-mohawk-repair-cable = Disabled M90: add ten lengths of cable (20 seconds).
cmu-mohawk-repair-weld = Disabled M90: weld the housing with a lit blowtorch (30 seconds, 5 fuel).
cmu-mohawk-repair-calibrate = Disabled M90: calibrate and close it with a screwdriver (20 seconds).
cmu-mohawk-repair-complete = M90 rebuild complete: restored to 2000 HP and ready for operation.
cmu-mohawk-free-fire-active = Stop AI free fire ({$seconds}s)
cmu-mohawk-free-fire-cooldown = AI free fire cooldown: {$seconds}s
cmu-mohawk-free-fire-help = Releases manual control and allows the AI to acquire and fire at IFF hostiles using the selected priority for 120 seconds. Groundside arc, range, slew, cover and friendly checks still apply. During a CAS flyby, first take control and select a signal flare; the AI engages only inside its ten-tile circle. The five-minute cooldown begins when free fire ends. Press again to stop early; taking manual control also ends free fire.
